Examiners (考試官):
Zuo Jing 左經, Assistant Instructor (訓導) of the Prefectural Confucian School (儒學) of Wuchang Prefecture 武昌府, Huguang [courtesy name Lüchang 履常, a native of Meizhou 眉州, Sichuan, and a Confucian Scholar (儒士)];
Zhu Shouxin 朱守信, Instructor (教諭) of the County Confucian School of Lanxi County 蘭谿縣, Jinhua Prefecture 金華府, Zhejiang [a native of Leping County 樂平縣, Raozhou Prefecture 饒州府, Jiangxi, and a Confucian Scholar].

Associate Examiners (同考試官):
Gao Lian 高璉, Instructor of the County Confucian School of Danyang County 丹陽縣, Zhenjiang Prefecture 鎮江府, Zhili [courtesy name Rulian 汝璉, a native of Yongfeng County 永豐縣, Ji'an Prefecture 吉安府, Jiangxi, and a Tribute Student (貢士) of the wuzi (1408) examination];
Chen Shi 陳實, Assistant Instructor of the County Confucian School of Yuhang County 餘杭縣, Hangzhou Prefecture 杭州府, Zhejiang [courtesy name Yuanfu 原夫, a native of Anren County 安仁縣, Raozhou Prefecture 饒州府, Jiangxi, and a Provincial Tribute Student (鄉貢士) of the jimao (1399) examination];
Jiang Bingxin 江秉心, Assistant Instructor of the County Confucian School of Changshan County 常山縣, Quzhou Prefecture 衢州府, Zhejiang [a native of Kaihua County 開化縣, Quzhou Prefecture 衢州府, Zhejiang, and a Confucian Scholar].

Examination Paper Custodians (收掌試卷官): …

One question to be answered from among the Edict, Patent, and Memorial

Edict: Imitating an edict by Emperor Zhang of Han (Han Zhangdi) to officials of the two-thousand-bushel rank encouraging agriculture and sericulture.

Patent: Imitating a patent by Emperor Taizong of Tang (Tang Taizong) appointing Dai Zhou 戴胄 as Vice Minister of the Court of Judicial Review.

Memorial: Imitating a memorial by Kong Yingda 孔穎達 of the Tang presenting the Correct Meaning of the Five Classics (Wujing zhengyi).

Five Legal Judgments:
Unauthorized dispatch of incumbent officials;
Stealing soldiers with blank travel permits [?];
Monopolizing the payment of tax grain;
Soliciting favors in official business;
Manufacturing not in accordance with regulations.

Third Session
Five Policy Questions

